Well, the representative of Manwe and Elbereth, to be more
precise.  While it is true that nothing in Silmarillion or
LOTR indicates this, if you read Unfinished Tales, page 398,
it indicates which valar sent which istari:

Aule:                        Curumo    (Saruman the White)
Orome:                       Alatar    (blue#1)
Manwe and Varda (Elbereth):  Olorin    (Gandalf the Grey)
Yavana:                      Aiwendil  (Radagast the Brown)
Mandos, Nienna, Orome:       Pallando  (blue#2)

Manwe and Elbereth both spoke up, urging Olorin (Gandalf)
to go, but he was afraid, and didn't want to.  Too bad,
they said, go anyway.  In short, he got drafted.  :-)

But his fears were misplaced, because he turned out to
be the most effective of the lot, anyway.

Of course, he was aided in his endeavours because on
arrival in Middle Earth, Cirdan perceived in him the
greatest spirit of all the istari, and gifted to him
the blessed +7 Ring of Fire.  (Which explains what
Gandalf meant when he told the balrog "I am a servant
of the secret fire".)  As all nethackers know, a good
magic ring is truly a blessing.

